        "message": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "thinking",
              "thinking": "Let me work through this classic problem carefully.\n\nLet b = price of the ball\nLet bat = price of the bat\n\nFrom the problem:\n1. bat + ball = $1.10\n2. bat = ball + $1.00\n\nSubstituting equation 2 into equation 1:\n(ball + $1.00) + ball = $1.10\n2(ball) + $1.00 = $1.10\n2(ball) = $0.10\nball = $0.05\n\nLet me verify:\n- Ball costs $0.05\n- Bat costs $0.05 + $1.00 = $1.05\n- Total: $0.05 + $1.05 = $1.10 \u2713\n\nThe ball costs **$0.05** (or 5 cents).",
              "signature": ""
            }
          ]
        },
